{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS4GPkvTj2TCdD42DBYY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've added all six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` to the registration and offers screens, sent through `Analytics.capture` with names and property types exactly as in the spec. `dart format` and `flutter analyze` both come back clean. I haven't run the app or checked that the events arrive in PostHog, and nothing was sent to any external service. Nothing is committed yet.\n\n**Registration screen** (`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart`):\n- **`registration_email_started` / `registration_phone_started`:** sent on the first character typed, once per visit to the screen. The email and phone values themselves are never sent.\n- **`loan_amount_changed`:** sent when the user lets go of the slider, with `amount` as a whole number.\n- **`terms_accepted`:** sent only when the box is ticked; unticking sends nothing.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped`:** sent just before going to the offers screen, with `amount` and `terms`.\n\n**Offers screen** (`lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`): it now has to remember scroll position, so I changed it to a stateful widget; it looks the same. `offers_scrolled` is sent when a scroll stops, but only if the user has got further down than before on this visit. The highest `offset` in a session is therefore their deepest scroll.\n\n**Decisions to check:**\n- **Event volume:** because you're on the PostHog free tier, I didn't take \"moved the slider\" and \"scrolled\" literally. Sending on every movement would mean dozens of events per gesture. If product wants every movement tracked, that's a quick change.\n- **`terms` is always `true`:** the Continue button stays disabled until terms are accepted. I still send it because the spec asks for it.\n\nThe Flutter tools kept adding a block of settings to `analysis_options.yaml` each time they ran. I undid that and deleted the generated `.dart_tool/` and `pubspec.lock`, so only the two screens changed, plus the new `ANSWER.md`, which has the full write-up."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":236,"cache_read_input_tokens":30238,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":236},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cd467c3-10a3-4c06-a095-c79e2a893327","uuid":"e93119ee-23d3-46d1-8445-9b3f1ab4c61c","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:47:40.722Z","request_id":"req_011CgS4GPW3qccKTM6BUqWEW"}
